 "title": "The offense's 11, and what \"11 personnel\" means",
 "html": "<p><strong>The fixed part:</strong> every offense has 11 players. Six never change jobs: five <strong>offensive linemen</strong> (left tackle, left guard, center, right guard, right tackle) who only block, and the <strong>quarterback</strong> (QB), who takes the snap from the center.</p>\n<p><strong>The flexible part:</strong> the other five are \"skill players,\" and the coach picks the mix for each play from three types:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Running back (RB):</strong> lines up behind or beside the QB and carries the ball on runs. Also catches short passes and blocks blitzers.</li>\n<li><strong>Fullback (FB):</strong> a second, bigger back whose main job is to run ahead of the RB and block the first defender in the way. Many NFL teams barely use one anymore, which is why you rarely see it.</li>\n<li><strong>Tight end (TE):</strong> lines up right next to a tackle. Half blocker, half receiver.</li>\n<li><strong>Wide receiver (WR):</strong> lines up wide, near the sideline (\"outside\") or between the line and the outside receiver (the \"slot\"). Catches passes.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"diagram\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"11 personnel in shotgun: five linemen, quarterback, one running back, one tight end, three wide receivers\"><defs><marker id=\"m1w\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/></marker><marker id=\"m1y\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"0\" x2=\"400\" y1=\"100\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#F2B705\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"6\" y=\"95\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.75)\">line of scrimmage</text><text x=\"202\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">offensive line: 5 blockers, never catch passes</text><rect x=\"139.0\" y=\"103.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"117\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">LT</text><rect x=\"165.0\" y=\"103.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"176\" y=\"117\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">LG</text><rect x=\"191.0\" y=\"103.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"202\" y=\"117\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">C</text><rect x=\"217.0\" y=\"103.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"228\" y=\"117\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">RG</text><rect x=\"243.0\" y=\"103.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"254\" y=\"117\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">RT</text><circle cx=\"286\" cy=\"116\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"286\" y=\"119.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">TE</text><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"114\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"117.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">WR</text><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"120\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"96\" y=\"123.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">WR</text><circle cx=\"372\" cy=\"114\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"372\" y=\"117.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">WR</text><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"168\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"202\" y=\"171.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">QB</text><circle cx=\"234\" cy=\"168\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"234\" y=\"171.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">RB</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"142\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">outside</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"148\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">slot</text><text x=\"372\" y=\"142\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">outside</text><text x=\"286\" y=\"144\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">tight end</text><text x=\"202\" y=\"196\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">shotgun: QB about 5 yds back, RB beside him</text></svg></div><p class=\"note\"><strong>11 personnel</strong> (1 RB, 1 TE, so 3 WR). The most common grouping in the NFL.</p><div class=\"diagram\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 222\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"21 personnel in the I-formation: quarterback under center with a fullback and running back stacked behind him, one tight end, two wide receivers\"><defs><marker id=\"m2w\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/></marker><marker id=\"m2y\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"0\" x2=\"400\" y1=\"100\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#F2B705\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"6\" y=\"95\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.75)\">line of scrimmage</text><rect x=\"139.0\" y=\"103.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"117\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">LT</text><rect x=\"165.0\" y=\"103.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"176\" y=\"117\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">LG</text><rect x=\"191.0\" y=\"103.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"202\" y=\"117\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">C</text><rect x=\"217.0\" y=\"103.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"228\" y=\"117\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">RG</text><rect x=\"243.0\" y=\"103.0\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"254\" y=\"117\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">RT</text><circle cx=\"286\" cy=\"116\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"286\" y=\"119.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">TE</text><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"114\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"117.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">WR</text><circle cx=\"372\" cy=\"114\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"372\" y=\"117.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">WR</text><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"140\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"202\" y=\"143.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">QB</text><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"168\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"202\" y=\"171.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">FB</text><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"198\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><text x=\"202\" y=\"201.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">RB</text><text x=\"218\" y=\"143\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">under center</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"169\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">fullback: blocks for the RB</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"201\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">running back: carries the ball</text><text x=\"202\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.9)\">the two backs stacked behind the QB = the \"I\"</text></svg></div><p class=\"note\"><strong>21 personnel</strong> (2 backs, one of them the FB, plus 1 TE, so 2 WR). A power-running look.</p>\n<p><strong>The naming code:</strong> first digit = backs (RB + FB), second digit = tight ends. Subtract both from 5 to get the receivers. 11 = 1 back, 1 TE, 3 WR. 12 = 1 back, 2 TE, 2 WR. 21 = 2 backs, 1 TE, 2 WR.</p>\n<p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> the defense sees who jogs onto the field before every play and sends in its own matching players (Lesson 2). More blockers (TEs, a FB) usually means the offense wants to run. More receivers usually means it wants to pass. The offense's trick is to show one and do the other.</p>\n<p><strong>How to spot it on TV:</strong> right before the snap, count players touching the line next to a tackle (TEs), then players behind the QB (backs). Everyone split out is a WR.</p>\n<p class=\"note\">Next: the defense's 11, and how \"base\" and \"nickel\" answer these groupings.</p>",
